              "text": "While I cannot directly process payments or book tickets for you, I can help you find the best options and provide the exact steps and direct links to secure your return ticket. \n\nSince today is Sunday, June 7, 2026, **\"next Friday\" refers to June 12, 2026**.\n\nTo buy a round-trip ticket from Boston to New York, follow the steps below:\n\n### 1. Choose Your Train Type\nAmtrak offers two primary options for this route departing from **Boston South Station (BOS)** or **Back Bay (BBY)** and arriving at **New York Penn Station / Moynihan Train Hall (NYP)**:\n*   **Northeast Regional:** The budget-friendly choice. It takes about **4 hours and 15 minutes**. One-way coach fares typically start around $50\u2013$150 when booked closer to the travel date.\n*   **Acela:** The high-speed, premium option. It takes about **3 hours and 35 minutes**. Fares are usually higher but offer more spacious seating and fewer stops.\n\n### 2. How to Book Your Tickets\nYou can easily complete your booking on the official **[Amtrak Website](https://www.amtrak.com)** or by downloading the **[Amtrak Mobile App](https://www.amtrak.com/amtrak-app)**. \n\n**Step-by-step to book:**\n1. Go to the **[Amtrak Fare Finder](https://www.amtrak.com)**.\n2. Select **Round Trip**.\n3. Input **Boston, MA (BOS)** as your departure station. \n4. Input **New York, NY (NYP)** as your arrival station.\n5. Set your departure date to **Friday, June 12, 2026**.\n6. Set your return date to your preferred day (for example, *Sunday, June 14, 2026* if you are staying for the weekend).\n7. Select your preferred train times, choose your seats, and complete your purchase securely.\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Important Travel Tip for June 2026\nPlease note that due to the **2026 FIFA World Cup**, there are modified access guidelines and increased security at Boston South Station effective from **June 11 to July 9, 2026**. It is highly recommended to **arrive at the station earlier than usual** for your Friday departure to navigate potential crowds and security sweeps.",
